{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And all the hills that were dug with a hoe, etc.</b> The vineyards that were there originally will now be restored, for there will be no thorns there, and so greatly will HaShem bestow blessing upon the hill vineyards that they will send the ox there, like the sense of 'I will lead my donkey to the vine' (Genesis 49:11). And behold, he said that one pen and two sheep will yield abundant milk, and the hill vineyards [conj. ובכרמי] that alone survive — HaShem will bestow blessing upon them beyond measure."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads וכרמי but the likely correct reading (noted צ״ל) is ובכרמי, 'and in the vineyards.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:43.481089264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}